<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thaya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dyje</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thaya (Czech Dyje) is a river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, about 235 kilometres long. Rising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-austria">Lower Austria</a>, it flows through southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/znojmo">Znojmo</a> and for long stretches forms the Austrian-Czech border. It joins the Morava near the meeting point of Austria, the Czech Republic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thaya.jpg" alt="Thaya" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fredericus · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B%C5%99eclav,_Dyje.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
